{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#115","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#115","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#115\",\"parent_revision\":\"a3e52a4e54d33331344955af1720a1f3834a460187a16921d6e6c447a992fd4a\",\"root_revision\":\"a3e52a4e54d33331344955af1720a1f3834a460187a16921d6e6c447a992fd4a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Observed Twice\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn agent dispatched with worktree isolation received a worktree based on `main` rather than the branch named in its brief. First occurrence reintroduced deleted code into a rules refactor. Second occurrence was caught only because the brief carried a manual first-step check and the agent obeyed it:\\n\\n```\\n$ git merge-base HEAD refactor/complete-rule-functions\\nfbc35365697cff850d1f9350326e234fc9360c2c     # == main tip, not the branch\\n$ git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...refactor/complete-rule-functions\\n2       17\\n```\\n\\nThe gap was 17 commits rewriting the exact two files in scope \u2014 `plugin_validator.py` was 5951 lines in the worktree versus 4452 on the requested branch. Committing from that base and merging would have reintroduced ~1770 deleted lines.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssert the requested ref is an ancestor of the new worktree HEAD at creation time, and fail loudly otherwise. A prose instruction in the brief is not a control \u2014 it works only when the agent both reads and obeys it, and the first occurrence shows what happens when one does not.\\n\\nExplicit creation works today and can serve as the interim path:\\n\\n```\\ngit worktree add <path> <branch>\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBriefs anchored on raw line numbers compound this. Three of four anchors in the second occurrence's brief were already wrong for the actual checkout, and the one that matched did so by coincidence \u2014 which reads as corroboration that the base is correct. Anchoring on symbol name plus containing module surfaces a wrong-base condition on the first grep.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d93faa7a613f5e5853229996aa6e981d5831b6cad4e75abab0ebfa068f14ff49\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-2nw\"}"}